      "dcterms:format": "application/json",
      "dcterms:description": "{\"action\":\"\",\"actor\":\"\",\"alternative_quotes\":[],\"applies_to\":[],\"assertion_ids\":[\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:907f3ed59b2e67fe1d061763662d754d7c80df927ae12ee63c8cb3e1ae01f621\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:a21bb6e597e9a8e3c70d18aaa14a473af3b3e0726a2390646635418c9ff92400\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:4c579ab65b7c5732524d83adbf51c4b8b6550dc7e1199e01944997f383f54dbf\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:585e446903b46bc0aabba7f14b680a897a3b456f938fb8f4daf724f378324962\",\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:15a63ec10d2dc0a19b8b2c1353afdfeb673b5bcc7ef1d67f06f633b5ca5deecb\"],\"choice_quote\":\"\",\"choice_text\":\"\",\"claimants\":[],\"concepts\":[],\"context_quotes\":[],\"effective_periods\":[],\"end\":408,\"evidence\":[{\"end\":408,\"field\":\"summary\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:86:408:sha256-450017904294f49b3cb28fae632c76405891b5fe06c0954feb39962aaafd7151\",\"quote\":\"a. A material discrepancy is any name change that is not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5. The applicant must explain any material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity (see 22 CFR 51.25).\",\"start\":86},{\"end\":408,\"field\":\"logic_text\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:86:408:sha256-450017904294f49b3cb28fae632c76405891b5fe06c0954feb39962aaafd7151\",\"quote\":\"a. A material discrepancy is any name change that is not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5. The applicant must explain any material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity (see 22 CFR 51.25).\",\"start\":86},{\"end\":201,\"field\":\"modality\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:197:201:sha256-4137b01e139589b7a1d3b3fc4da031d8ce5bb415808734e970c3a58ea0e98f0f\",\"quote\":\"must\",\"start\":197},{\"end\":408,\"field\":\"scope_text:0\",\"fragment_id\":\"urn:rkaf:fragment:urn%3Arulespec%3Adocument-understanding%3Adocument%3Aaa23cc4bc9758753066c6a970bc4e4d08f001f9fb228a7ab60b296a5ade86fdc:86:408:sha256-450017904294f49b3cb28fae632c76405891b5fe06c0954feb39962aaafd7151\",\"quote\":\"a. A material discrepancy is any name change that is not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5. The applicant must explain any material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity (see 22 CFR 51.25).\",\"start\":86}],\"id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:revision:f5c462022da35364971f712cdf36f888d57e4edf1ef9121cb8bc14691cf95025\",\"jurisdiction\":\"\",\"jurisdiction_quote\":\"\",\"kind\":\"requirement\",\"logic_text\":\"a. A material discrepancy is any name change that is not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5. The applicant must explain any material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity (see 22 CFR 51.25).\",\"meaning_assertion_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:assertion:15a63ec10d2dc0a19b8b2c1353afdfeb673b5bcc7ef1d67f06f633b5ca5deecb\",\"modality\":\"must\",\"modality_quote\":\"must\",\"object\":\"\",\"occurrence_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:occurrence:de5bb9de91a630900218594070c45bbb9c43fd8662b7ffec2c7ad9107bb9e52a\",\"origin\":\"aiSuggested\",\"quote\":\"a. A material discrepancy is any name change that is not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5. The applicant must explain any material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity (see 22 CFR 51.25).\",\"references\":[\"22 CFR 51.25\"],\"relation\":\"none\",\"rule_id\":\"urn:rulespec:document-understanding:rule:2d055da4fe779ef53f7d5c26997b47acd0e042c7d197a4b4009426b6f88c2fb2\",\"scope_quotes\":[\"a. A material discrepancy is any name change that is not defined as immaterial in 8 FAM 403.1-5. The applicant must explain any material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity (see 22 CFR 51.25).\"],\"scope_text\":\"When there are material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity.\",\"section_id\":\"fam-names-section-4\",\"start\":86,\"summary\":\"The applicant must explain any material discrepancies between the name on the application and the name recorded in the evidence of U.S. citizenship/non-citizen U.S. nationality and the evidence of identity (see 22 CFR 51.25).\",\"target_ids\":[],\"typed_values\":[]}",
